node_modules/
build/
dist/
vendor/
.env/
.venv/
.tox/
*.min.js
.npm/
.yarn/
# Common test paths
test/
tests/
testsuite/
*_test.go
# Semgrep rules folder
.semgrep
# Semgrep-action log folder
.semgrep_logs/

# --- This repository ---------------------------------------------------------
# Alembic revisions. Every finding Semgrep has ever produced here is one of two
# rules — sqlalchemy-execute-raw-query and formatted-sql-query — and both are
# structurally inapplicable to a migration:
#
#   * PostgreSQL cannot parameterize IDENTIFIERS. There is no bind-parameter form
#     of `ALTER TABLE <name>`, `CREATE POLICY <name>` or `DROP INDEX <name>`, so
#     "use parameterized queries instead" describes something the database does not
#     offer. The advice applies to query VALUES, which these statements do not take.
#   * Every interpolated value is a literal declared in the same file — module-level
#     tuples such as `_RLS_TABLES`, `_DOWNGRADE_DROPS` and `_TENANT_EXPRESSION`. No
#     request data, no function argument, nothing from the network reaches them.
#
# Scoped to the revision files, not to `migrations/` as a whole, so `env.py` and any
# future helper module here stay scanned. Confirmed against the exact image CI uses
# (semgrep/semgrep:1.97.0, --config=p/default): 148 findings in this directory, 148
# of them those two rules and nothing else — so this costs no real coverage.
#
# If a migration ever needs to interpolate something that is NOT a literal, that is
# the moment to delete this entry rather than widen it.
migrations/versions/
